{"test":"text:nat_en.txt","n_prompt":113,"pp_s":5.937,"pp_ts":19.0325,"n_gen":128,"tg_ts":6.7373,"tg_total_ts":6.7150,"gen":"The storm came in three waves. The first was a wall of water that lifted the lighthouse off its foundations and carried it out to sea. The second wave broke the light’s lens, and the third wave took the keeper’s life. When the sea finally calmed, the lighthouse was empty, the lamp still burning, and the logbook open to the page where the keeper had written, “The sea is angry.” The next morning, the coast guard found the lighthouse, but the keeper was gone, and the logbook was missing. The only clue was a single footprint in the sand, leading away from the lighthouse"}
